  (text "Based on github.com/mariosgit/VFD" (at 111.76 21.59 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 23012358-cab5-4256-a83d-3e45ca2a467c)
  )
  (text "Experiment Results\n--------------------------\n\n- using a slow self-oscillation was not successful,\n  and using the fast oscillation with VREF dimming\n  was suboptimal\n\n- I bodged the NAND chip to completely remove the\n  enable jumper and drive the oscillation externally\n  with a QT Py at ~ 250 Hz\n\n- Brightness trimming with RV1 works fabulously!\n\n- A center tap diode / capacitive coupling for the\n  filament does not seem to be necessary .. since the\n  lowest voltage with an H-Bridge is always GND, the\n  ghosting effect is only veeery dim.\n\n- I used 0Ω jumpers for R16, R17. Should keep the\n  footprints anyway, just in case."
    (at 121.92 127 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 9522cca1-9761-42e6-b0ab-b3f832da379e)
  )
  (text "Frequency via R15+C11: http://www.eedesignonline.com/STO.html\n 10nF,  10kΩ ~  25 kHz\n100nF, 100kΩ ~ 250  Hz (Bridge Driver in VRef PWM recom. max. 400 Hz)\n 10nF, 2.2kΩ ~  27 kHz (experimental result)"
    (at 162.56 74.93 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 2eb0d53d-1652-4512-a6b0-be8c08f13da4)
  )
  (text "(alt: BD6211F-E2, BA6287F-E2)" (at 217.17 63.5 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid e40624dc-9acd-4696-a441-4bd9525bb7c8)
  )
